		<div class="story-heads">
		<h1>Paul Yoon, Meaghan Beatley, Claudia Rankine, and more: 22 new books out today!</h1>
			</div>
	</div>
										<div class="byline-date">
					<span class="byline"><a href="https://lithub.com/author/juliahass/"  title="Julia Hass">Julia Hass</a></span>
					<span class="hr"></span>
					<span class="date">August 4, 2026</span>
				</div>
						<div class="story-body">
								<p style="text-align: left;">The first week of August brings a windfall of heavyweight literature: a novel by Paul Yoon, a searing nonfiction book of essays by Meaghan Beatley, and a much anticipated work by Claudia Rankine. This is just the beginning: read on for the full selection of books available today, and happy reading!</p><div class="insert-post-ads" style="clear:both;width:100%;margin:0 0 20px 0;"><span>Article continues after advertisement</span><script id="861f6ebfff7b44919831c03590113e1a">(new Image()).src = 'https://capi.connatix.com/tr/si?token=546998bb-b9c0-4480-8c91-3e307220efff&cid=86b7c382-5e20-4129-84db-dea768f4d688';  cnx.cmd.push(function() {    cnx({      playerId: "546998bb-b9c0-4480-8c91-3e307220efff"    }).render("861f6ebfff7b44919831c03590113e1a");  });</script></div>
<p style="text-align: center;">*</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="274409" data-permalink="https://lithub.com/etna/attachment/9781668020821/" data-orig-file="https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821.jpg" data-orig-size="778,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}" data-image-title="etna paul yoon" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821-664x1024.jpg" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-274409" src="https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821-195x300.jpg" alt="etna paul yoon" width="195" height="300" srcset="https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821-195x300.jpg 195w, https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821-664x1024.jpg 664w, https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821-768x1185.jpg 768w, https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821-39x60.jpg 39w, https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821-32x50.jpg 32w, https://s26162.pcdn.co/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/9781668020821.jpg 778w" sizes="(max-width: 195px) 100vw, 195px" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Paul Yoon, <a href="https://bookshop.org/a/40/9781668020821" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="external"><em>Etna</em></a></strong><br />
<strong>(Scribner)</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">“In this masterful and infinitely moving dog’s tale, Yoon shows us what great fiction can do: change the way we see the world by sharing the song of another heart.&#8221;<br />
<em>–</em>Mona Awad</p>
